  ('LBN-TAX-007', 'Law 360', 'Foreigners can acquire 3% of total Lebanon area (up to 10% in Beirut); 3,000m2 without Council of Ministers decree', 'en', 'Real Estate Registration and Transfer Tax Law, Article Law 360', 'Foreign Acquisition Limits', 'Tax Law'),
  ('LBN-TAX-007', 'Law 360', 'Permettre aux étrangers d''acquérir 3% de la superficie totale du Liban', 'fr', 'Real Estate Registration and Transfer Tax Law, Article Law 360', 'Foreign Acquisition Limits', 'Tax Law'),
  ('LBN-TAX-007', 'Law 360', 'السماح للأجانب بشراء 3% من مساحة لبنان الكلية', 'ar', 'Real Estate Registration and Transfer Tax Law, Article Law 360', 'Foreign Acquisition Limits', 'Tax Law'),
  ('LBN-TAX-007', NULL, 'Law 296/2001 was a major reform to encourage foreign real estate investment by simplifying ownership rules and reducing fees. Law 360/2001 further liberalized foreign acquisition limits. The 2018 amendment provided temporary reductions for residential properties.', 'en', 'Real Estate Registration and Transfer Tax Law — Historical Context', 'Historical context and overview', 'Tax Law'),
  ('LBN-TAX-008', 'General Provisions', 'Excise taxes apply to alcoholic beverages, tobacco products, gasoline, and vehicles', 'en', 'Excise Taxes, Article General Provisions', 'Taxable Products', 'Tax Law'),
  ('LBN-TAX-008', 'General Provisions', 'Taxes d''accise sur les boissons alcoolisées, le tabac et les carburants', 'fr', 'Excise Taxes, Article General Provisions', 'Taxable Products', 'Tax Law'),
  ('LBN-TAX-008', 'General Provisions', 'الضرائب الانتقائية على المشروبات الكحولية والتبغ والوقود', 'ar', 'Excise Taxes, Article General Provisions', 'Taxable Products', 'Tax Law'),
  ('LBN-TAX-008', NULL, 'Excise taxes in Lebanon are primarily applied to ''sin goods'' and luxury items. Rates are adjusted annually through Budget Laws.', 'en', 'Excise Taxes — Historical Context', 'Historical context and overview', 'Tax Law'),
